A turn on spare time ends at a call that stopped for an interrupt,
so another thread runs before the call is made again.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a call stopped where its caller cannot make it again
Witness: fuzz spare-turn-waits-for-recall

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -1255,7 +1255,7 @@ static bool deadline_due(struct core *core)
  */
 static void spare_end(struct core *core)
 {
-    if (core->run_queue != 0 && !core->recall && (sched_spare_turn(core) || deadline_due(core))) {
+    if (core->run_queue != 0 && (sched_spare_turn(core) || deadline_due(core))) {
         sched_turn_end();
     }
 }
